              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Telugu for a march, then the Telugu for to march against."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: తక్షణం",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "తక్షణం — takṣaṇaṁ — \"instantly; at once\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "సాక్షి తక్షణం పోలీసులకు ఫోను చేశాడు. sākṣi takṣaṇaṁ pōlīsulaku phōnu cēśāḍu. The witness phoned the police at once."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Literally that very moment: తత్ and క్షణం. తక్షణమే is stronger still. Where ఈలోగా, meanwhile, leaves a little time, తక్షణం (takṣaṇaṁ) leaves none."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "తక్షణం (takṣaṇaṁ) is borrowed from Sanskrit tatkṣaṇam, \"at that very moment\", from tad, \"that\", and kṣaṇa, \"a moment\" (CDIAL 5640)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "takṣaṇaṁ",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *takṣaṇaṁ*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "takṣaṇaṁ, once more",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *takṣaṇaṁ*, once more]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "sākṣi takṣaṇaṁ pōlīsulaku phōnu cēśāḍu. — The witness phoned the police at once.",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *sākṣi takṣaṇaṁ pōlīsulaku phōnu cēśāḍu.* — The witness phoned the police at once.]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "RECALL",
              "instruction": "say the Telugu for a march, then the Telugu for to march against, then say takṣaṇaṁ again",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU RECALL: say the Telugu for a march, then the Telugu for to march against, then say *takṣaṇaṁ* again]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 5,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
