          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "తీరా — tīrā — \"in the end; when it came to it\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "చాలా రోజులు వెతికాము, తీరా అది ఇంట్లోనే ఉంది. cālā rōjulu vetikāmu, tīrā adi iṇṭlōnē undi. We searched for days, and in the end it was right at home."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A spoken word that brings a surprise ending, often an ironic one."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "తీరా (tīrā) is native Dravidian, built on tīru, \"to be finished, concluded\" (DEDR 3278): when everything was done."
            }
          ]
        },
